  "findings": [
    "With the trained OOF head as the consultant on every rung, the ladder DOES NOT hold at any top-k in 15-35: the loop's best validation-selected value (n=20, 0.8269) still sits below AGAF (0.8331) and below the LLM head it consults (0.8321).",
    "Retuning top_k for the head recovered +0.0059 over the carried-over n=16 (0.8210 -> 0.8269) and narrowed loop-AGAF from -0.0126 to -0.0067, but did not flip the sign.",
    "No candidate n reaches the LLM head on validation-selected terms; the best test value in the whole sweep (n=33, 0.8312) is still below the head, and selecting it would require test labels.",
    "Validation macro-F1 is nearly flat across n (0.8265-0.8312, spread 0.0047), so top_k is not the binding constraint under the head consultant.",
    "AGAF-head and LLM-head are separated by 0.0010 (CI [0.0000, 0.0033]) - AGAF adds essentially nothing over its own consultant, which is degenerate rather than a result.",
    "head_only ablation (0.5578377548169227) is bit-identical across every head run and the prototype run, as expected: that mode sets fusion_emb = None so the GNN logits pass through untouched."
  ],
